<title>USA: Martin Industries adopts reinvestment plan.</title>
<headline>Martin Industries adopts reinvestment plan.</headline>
<dateline>FLORENCE, Ala. 1997-05-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Martin Industries Inc said on Wednesday that its directors had adopted a dividend reinvestment and direct stock purchase plan, providing a way for shareholders to increase their equity in the company.</p>
<p>The company said it had reserved 200,000 shares for the plan, that will be administered by AmSouth Bank of Alabama.</p>
<p>Martin expects the plan to be effective for the second quarter dividend, which is payable in the third quarter of 1997.</p>
<p>Martin Industries manufactures and sells gas and solid fuel heaters, fireplaces and barbecue grills.</p>
